WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.916 --> 00:00:09.463
Adam going to work with Mom for the day.

2
00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:14.747
"Delivering mail will be fun," said Adam.

3
00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:18.590
"A lot more fun than learning stuff at school."

4
00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:23.955
"You're going to work hard," said Mom.

5
00:00:23.975 --> 00:00:29.980
"And you'll still be learning—all about helping customers."

6
00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:34.433
"That sounds better than learning about fractions!"

7
00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:35.373
said Adam.

8
00:00:40.515 --> 00:00:43.976
At the post office, Adam and Mom filled two large mailbags.

9
00:00:47.197 --> 00:00:50.498
Then they drove to a busy neighborhood to deliver the letters and packages.

10
00:00:56.479 --> 00:00:58.100
Adam wiped sweat from his forehead.

11
00:00:59.612 --> 00:01:01.574
"My mailbag is so heavy.

12
00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.555
When's morning recess?"

13
00:01:05.236 --> 00:01:05.897
Mom chuckled.

14
00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:09.879
"There's no recess when you're working!"

15
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:10.820
she said.

16
00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.342
"But later we'll take a short lunch break."

17
00:01:15.443 --> 00:01:16.804
She pointed up a steep hill.

18
00:01:16.824 --> 00:01:18.405
"Follow me!"

19
00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:23.669
At the top of the hill, Adam carried a package to a house.

20
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.051
"Woof! Woof!"

21
00:01:26.491 --> 00:01:27.752
A dog barked from inside.

22
00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:32.329
"Shh, Peanut!"

23
00:01:32.789 --> 00:01:33.369
said a woman.

24
00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:39.312
She opened the door wider to get her mail—and the dog dashed outside.

25
00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:42.553
"Oh no!

26
00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.394
My precious Peanut!"

27
00:01:44.794 --> 00:01:45.495
cried the woman.

28
00:01:46.635 --> 00:01:48.596
Peanut charged after a garbage truck.

29
00:01:48.616 --> 00:01:52.518
"I'll get him!"

30
00:01:52.838 --> 00:01:54.759
Adam yelled, running after the dog.

31
00:01:56.119 --> 00:01:57.200
They raced down the hill.

32
00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:04.517
Peanut chased a butterfly and a skateboarder.

33
00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.621
Finally he stopped to sniff a fire hydrant.

34
00:02:14.663 --> 00:02:15.383
Adam pounced.

35
00:02:15.403 --> 00:02:20.666
"Gotcha!" When Adam came back with Peanut, he was huffing and puffing.

36
00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:28.450
job," Mom said.

37
00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:31.292
"Now back to work!"

38
00:02:32.808 --> 00:02:34.468
Adam groaned and followed his mother.

39
00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.390
Their last delivery was on Chestnut Street.

40
00:02:43.231 --> 00:02:45.391
Adam started to put letters into the mailbox.

41
00:02:48.852 --> 00:02:50.873
A man stomped angrily toward them.

42
00:02:52.533 --> 00:02:54.014
"My mail is late!"

43
00:02:54.414 --> 00:02:54.994
he growled.

44
00:02:55.014 --> 00:02:58.715
"I've been waiting all afternoon!"

45
00:02:58.735 --> 00:03:01.256
"Very sorry, sir!"

46
00:03:01.576 --> 00:03:02.576
said Mom politely.

47
00:03:05.988 --> 00:03:08.070
Adam and Mom drove back to the post office.

48
00:03:09.471 --> 00:03:11.292
"That man was rude, Mom."

49
00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:14.394
Mom shrugged.

50
00:03:14.414 --> 00:03:16.816
"Mail carriers have to be polite.

51
00:03:17.276 --> 00:03:18.797
That's a big part of the job."

52
00:03:24.161 --> 00:03:26.102
At home Adam fell onto the sofa.

53
00:03:26.122 --> 00:03:29.765
"Phew!" "Tired?"

54
00:03:30.265 --> 00:03:30.905
asked Mom.

55
00:03:30.925 --> 00:03:34.448
"Yes!" said Adam.

56
00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.125
"Working was fun, but I can't wait to get back to school!"
